From 66a4d4d2c36010bff5b6a3a5c3f60dcbc8a6d1d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:26:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] coreclr: C++ sources for clang with the GNU driver

MSVC accepts these, clang does not, or the Windows code paths key on
_MSC_VER where they mean the Windows SDK/LLP64:
- functions converted to void* implicitly (ComInterfaceSlotIs,
  GetMemoryRangeForFunction take any function pointer; casts at the
  GetProcAddress and hijack-target sites);
- gotos past initializations (peimagelayout, threadsuspend);
- copy-initialization through a private copy constructor (AllocMemHolder);
- ULONG overloads of AlignUp/AlignDown, the BitScan* wrappers of the JIT,
  JITINTERFACE_HRESULT = long, GET_UNALIGNED_* also with MinGW;
- the dummy VPTR constructors of daccess.h for the DAC table (as on Unix:
  no /ALTERNATENAME), a default CodeRangeMapRangeList constructor for them;
- forward-declared enums without a type, an enumerator that does not fit,
  the address of a temporary, an ambiguous conditional, invalid token
  pastes, _alloca/__report_gsfailure/roerrorapi.h declarations;
- the GS cookie seeded without MSVC's __security_cookie;
- gcenv.windows.cpp's g_SystemInfo static (Itanium does not mangle
  variable types, so it clashed with the VM's SYSTEM_INFO g_SystemInfo);
- mingw-w64's JOBOBJECT_CPU_RATE_CONTROL_INFORMATION lacks MaxRate.
